Z||000000||Predator||12-22-2000||09:57 PM||||Ok guys please humor me here. I may be just overly causious with my car here. I recently installed a Turbo from Design1Systems. I drove the car a while and now it looks like a lot of smoke is coming out the back. I already asked this question, but I have a little more information.1fst2m6 is coming over on the 30th to help diagnose what or if there is a problem. It is cold so it could be from that maybe. The car runs fine, no knocking, the oil and water level is fine. It is a burning smelling kind of smoke if that helps. It is not the black oil smoke. It is not as white as it was when I first saw it. The engine revs fine, and does not misfire or show any signs of problems. The guages all read normal, and I checked the computer and I have no error codes. It cranks right up as well. It is smoking a lot though,and that is bothering me. The turbo guage rises and falls mormal, and I checked the oil lines and they are getting oil to the turbo. I am stumped on this. Am I going crazy here, and the only problem is in my head, or does someone else think this is a problem. Thanks guys I know this sounds wierd. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||12-22-2000||10:20 PM||||Have you checked with D1? they may coat the pipes with Wax type stuf to prevent rust at the factory, so if you havent goten on it yet to bring the system up to full running temp. It wont have melted off yet. <P>   this happend then I instaled a new 3" exhaust system no my truck it scared the hell outa me for a week until I took it back to the shop they raged on it a bit and it was fine.<P>*****DISCLAMER!!!***** let Travis look at it B4 you go Kill your car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> in case somethingis wrong pluss I'd fell like crap if some thing did happen||||reg||1
