Z||000005||gixxer||12-22-2000||11:02 PM||||None of the Design 1 tubes uses a varnish coating, altho there is a slight oil film on it(it's all stainless).<BR>From the "Maximum Boost" book:<BR>"Blue Smoke" (whitish-blue oil out the tailpipes) trouble symptom.<BR>(I edited the list assuming you are using the new parts supplied in the kit.)<BR>* Plugged crankcase breather.<BR>* Collapsed or restricted air tube before the turbo.<BR>* Foreign object between air cleaner and turbo.<BR>* Turbo flanges, clamps or bolts loose.<BR>* Inlet manifold cracked, gaskets loose or missing, connections loose.<BR>* Restricted oil drain line.<BR>* Turbo seal leakage.<BR>* Excessive engine pre-oil.<BR>* Excessive engine idle (?)<BR>* Leaking valve stem seals.<BR>Let us know what you find in any event.<BR>Thanx<BR>  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Xtreme Fiero's||12-22-2000||11:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Predator:<BR><B>I have driven it maybe 30 or 40 miles.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I withdraw my prevous post And wish you luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Philphine||12-23-2000||01:17 AM||||running rich maybe? fuel reg. adjustment? the extra compression blowing out carbon? some kind of oil leak at the turbo that is becoming part of the intake charge? half (1/4?,1/8?) educated guess since you feel it runs fine other wise. hope you find out and tell us the fix.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||12-23-2000||08:18 AM||||I have a turbo conversion myself. It does seem to have a  little more whitish 'smoke' when its really cold out(like your hot breath in the cold). I just think its because some of the exhaust heat is transfered to the intake air, its always done it when its cold on mine. Could very well be all you have there, expecially since you dont have any bad symtoms. I do know that I have to adjust my wastegate when it gets down below 30* or I get overboost.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=35934618"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||12-23-2000||05:07 PM||||Check your spark plugs. They are the best indicators of what is going in the cylinders.<P>Pictures <A HREF="http://www.centuryperformance.com/spark2.htm#Normal" TARGET=_blank>http://www.centuryperformance.com/spark2.htm#Normal</A>  Condition ||||reg||1
